       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter one of these instead:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is the usual dose for pain or fever.\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO once or twice daily**, if the 1600 mg figure was meant as a total daily dose. Say which you intend.\n\nDid you mean one of these, perhaps 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day) or 800 mg four times daily? If you want a different drug or a different approach, tell me and I'll enter that."
