       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the numbers. I can't verify the label claim, and it doesn't match what I know of the labeling. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The FDA-approved prescription label sets the maximum at 3,200 mg/day, and a single dose shouldn't go above 800 mg. The OTC maximum is lower still, at 1,200 mg/day.\n\nIf the label you're looking at says something different, please check it again. It may be listing 3,200 mg/day as the total.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose)\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day, which may be what you meant by 1600)\n\nIf the patient needs more analgesia than the maximum ibuprofen dose gives, I can enter a multimodal option instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen. Tell me which you'd like."
      }
     ],
